<!-- TEST 2026-08-21: consolidated single-shell Hangar, random-plane-via-SpawnGroup-selection mechanism.
     Untested in this project — no prior SpawnGroup here combines two independent prefabs.
     Position offset pulled from the old combined NPC-WW2-Hangar-FC20.sbc's baked plane-grid
     position relative to the hangar grid's own (0,0,0) origin. Orientation is NOT set here —
     the schema only exposes Position per sub-prefab, so the plane will spawn in its own
     Player-WW2-FC20 blueprint's default facing, which may not match the hangar's interior
     rotation. Expect this to need correction after an in-game look.
     Once confirmed working, this replaces all four per-plane Hangar SpawnGroups above and the
     old combined per-plane Hangar-*.sbc prefabs become unused.

     CORRECTION PASS 2026-08-21, after first in-game test: user reported the Hangar shell itself
     spawned 1.2 large blocks too low (floor under the ground) and FC20 spawned 8 large blocks too
     low, 13 too far forward, and 9.5 too far right (relative to the hangar, looking at the doors
     from outside). Converted at 2.5m per large block: Hangar Y +3.0m. FC20 Y +20.0m.
     Horizontal axes assumed per SE's standard convention — Right=+X, Forward=-Z, Up=+Y — since
     this can't be verified from the XML alone: "too far right" corrected as X -23.75m (9.5 blocks
     toward -X/left), "too far forward" corrected as Z +32.5m (13 blocks toward +Z/backward). If
     either comes out backwards on the next test, it's a single sign flip on that axis, not a
     re-derivation.

     CORRECTION PASS 2, 2026-08-21: X was backwards — moving X negative moved FC20 further right,
     not left. Confirmed mapping is actually Right=-X (opposite of the standard-convention guess).
     Flipped the sign of the X correction only: went from -43.964599609375 back past the original
     -20.214599609375 to +3.535400390625 (original + 23.75 instead of original - 23.75). Y (height)
     and the plane's default orientation were both confirmed correct as-is — no changes there.
     Z (forward/back) was not flagged as wrong, so the Forward=-Z assumption stands unless a later
     test says otherwise.

     CORRECTION PASS 3, 2026-08-21: further tuning from the pass-2 result — Y +2.5m (up, confirmed
     direction), X -3.75m (right, per the pass-2-confirmed mapping that decreasing X moves right).
     Z left unchanged. User also reports FC20 now faces backwards relative to how it looked before
     the pass-2 X flip — NOT fixable via this SpawnGroup: vanilla's own documented SpawnGroup
     schema (SpawnGroups_CargoShips.sbc's header comment) confirms <Prefab> only supports
     Position/BeaconText/Speed, no per-prefab orientation field. The plane always spawns in its
     blueprint's own saved default facing; fixing this requires re-exporting Player-WW2-FC20's
     blueprint rotated correctly in-game, not a further position tweak here. Hold off on that
     until position is fully dialed in, to avoid re-exporting more than once. -->
	<SpawnGroup>
		<Id>
			<TypeId>SpawnGroupDefinition</TypeId>
			<SubtypeId>WW2-Hangar-Gray-FC20</SubtypeId>
		</Id>
		<Description>

		[Modular Encounters SpawnGroup]

		[PlanetaryInstallationType:Medium]

		[SpawnConditionsProfiles:WW2-SpawnConditions-Installations]
		[ManipulationProfiles:MES-Manipulation-RivalAi]

		[FactionOverride:GRAY]
		[SpawnRandomCargo:true]

		[UseContainerTypeAssignment:true]
		[ContainerTypeAssignBlockName:Small Cargo Container]
		[ContainerTypeAssignSubtypeId:WW2-SmallCargo]

		[ContainerTypeAssignBlockName:Medium Cargo Container]
		[ContainerTypeAssignSubtypeId:WW2-MediumCargo]

		</Description>
		<Frequency>1.0</Frequency>
		<IsPirate>true</IsPirate>
		<Prefabs>
			<Prefab SubtypeId="NPC-WW2-Hangar">
				<Position>
					<X>0.0</X>
					<Y>3.0</Y>
					<Z>0.0</Z>
				</Position>
				<Behaviour>WW2-Behavior-Hangar-Gray</Behaviour>
				<Speed>0.0</Speed>
			</Prefab>
			<Prefab SubtypeId="Player-WW2-FC20">
				<Position>
					<X>-0.214599609375</X>
					<Y>3.635345458984375</Y>
					<Z>10.076156616210938</Z>
				</Position>
				<Behaviour>WW2-Behavior-HangarPlane-FC20</Behaviour>
				<Speed>0.0</Speed>
			</Prefab>
		</Prefabs>
	</SpawnGroup>
<!-- End test spawn group -->

<!-- End Hangar Spawns -->

	</SpawnGroups>
</Definitions>